public with sharing class ContactLookupAction {

    @InvocableMethod(Label='Find Contact by Email', Description='Finds an existing Contact by email address.')
    public static List<Result> find(List<Request> requests) {
        List<Result> results = new List<Result>();
        if (requests == null) {
            return results;
        }

        Set<String> uniqueEmails = new Set<String>();
        for (Request req : requests) {
            if (req != null && req.email != null) {
                String normalized = req.email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (normalized.length() > 0) {
                    uniqueEmails.add(normalized);
                }
            }
        }

        Map<String, Contact> earliestByEmail = new Map<String, Contact>();
        if (!uniqueEmails.isEmpty()) {
            List<String> emailsToQuery = new List<String>(uniqueEmails);
            for (Contact c : [SELECT Id, CreatedDate, Email FROM Contact WHERE LOWER(Email) IN :emailsToQuery ORDER BY CreatedDate ASC, Id ASC]) {
                if (c.Email != null) {
                    String normalized = c.Email.toLowerCase();
                    if (!earliestByEmail.containsKey(normalized)) {
                        earliestByEmail.put(normalized, c);
                    }
                }
            }
        }

        for (Request req : requests) {
            Result r = new Result();
            r.found = false;
            r.contactId = null;
            if (req != null && req.email != null) {
                String normalized = req.email.trim().toLowerCase();
                if (normalized.length() > 0) {
                    Contact c = earliestByEmail.get(normalized);
                    if (c != null) {
                        r.contactId = c.Id;
                        r.found = true;
                    }
                }
            }
            results.add(r);
        }
        return results;
    }

    public class Request {
        @InvocableVariable(Label='Email', Description='Email address to search for.', Required=true)
        public String email;
    }

    public class Result {
        @InvocableVariable(Label='Contact ID', Description='Id of the earliest-created Contact with the email.')
        public Id contactId;
        @InvocableVariable(Label='Found', Description='True if a Contact was found.')
        public Boolean found;
    }
}
```

Looking at the errors, I identified three issues:

1. `isEmpty()` doesn't exist on `String` in Apex — must use `.length() == 0`
2. `map` is a **reserved keyword** in Apex (like `number`, `list`, `order`) — using it as a variable name breaks the parser, making it unable to parse the `Map<String, Object>` type on that line
3. `number` is also a reserved keyword — can't use it as a field name in an inner class for JSON serialization

I'll rename variables to avoid reserved words and use `JSONGenerator` for the acknowledgement output.

