public class CaseSurveyJob implements Queueable {
    private final List<Id> caseIds;

    // Single-case constructor (used by tests or direct enqueue)
    public CaseSurveyJob(Id caseId) {
        this.caseIds = new List<Id>{ caseId };
    }

    // Bulk constructor (used by the trigger / chaining)
    public CaseSurveyJob(List<Id> caseIds) {
        this.caseIds = caseIds;
    }

    public void execute(QueueableContext context) {
        if (caseIds.size() == 1) {
            // Leaf: create the Task for this single case
            createSurveyTask(caseIds[0]);
        } else {
            // Dispatcher: fan out into individual per-case jobs.
            // Governor limit: max 50 System.enqueueJob calls per transaction.
            // If we still have work remaining, reserve one slot for the
            // next chained dispatcher (49 jobs + 1 dispatcher = 50).
            Integer batchSize = (caseIds.size() > 50) ? 49 : caseIds.size();

            for (Integer i = 0; i < batchSize; i++) {
                System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(caseIds[i]));
            }

            if (caseIds.size() > batchSize) {
                List<Id> remaining = new List<Id>();
                for (Integer i = batchSize; i < caseIds.size(); i++) {
                    remaining.add(caseIds[i]);
                }
                System.enqueueJob(new CaseSurveyJob(remaining));
            }
        }
    }

    private void createSurveyTask(Id caseId) {
        Case c = [SELECT Id, CaseNumber, ContactId
                  FROM Case
                  WHERE Id = :caseId
                  LIMIT 1];

        if (c == null || c.ContactId == null) {
            return;
        }

        Task t = new Task(
            WhatId       = c.Id,
            WhoId        = c.ContactId,
            Subject      = 'CSAT survey: ' + c.CaseNumber,
            ActivityDate = Date.today().addDays(2),
            Status       = 'Not Started'
        );
        insert t;
    }
}
```

## What changed and why

1. **Removed the separate `CaseSurveyDispatcher` class** (only two files are allowed). The dispatcher logic is folded into `CaseSurveyJob` itself via a **self-chaining pattern**:

   - **Single-element list** (`size == 1`): the job acts as a *leaf*—it queries the Case and inserts the Task. This is the "one job per case" unit of work, giving full transactional isolation (one DmlException only rolls back that one Task).
   - **Multi-element list** (`size > 1`): the job acts as a *dispatcher*—it enqueues up to 49 single-element `CaseSurveyJob` instances. If more Ids remain, it enqueues one more `CaseSurveyJob` carrying the tail (49 + 1 = 50 calls, within the limit).

2. **Trigger enqueues a single job** with the full list of qualifying Ids. This avoids the `LimitException` on the 51st `System.enqueueJob` call when 200 cases are closed in one transaction.

3. **`List<Id>` sub-slicing done manually** (Apex `List` has no `sublist()` method). A loop builds the `remaining` list for the chained call.

### Trace for 200 cases

| Transaction | Role | Calls |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Dispatcher (200) | 49 leaf + 1 dispatcher(151) = 50 |
| 2 | Dispatcher (151) | 49 leaf + 1 dispatcher(102) = 50 |
| 3 | Dispatcher (102) | 49 leaf + 1 dispatcher(53) = 50 |
| 4 | Dispatcher (53) | 49 leaf + 1 dispatcher(4) = 50 |
| 5 | Dispatcher (4) | 4 leaf = 4 |

Total leaf jobs created: 49 × 4 + 4 = **200** ✓ — no `LimitException`, each case in its own transaction.

## Fix

`Messaging.SendEmailResult` only exposes `isSuccess()` and `getNumberOfErrors()`. There is no `getMessages()` returning a list of detail objects, and `Messaging.StatusDetail` is not a valid type. I'll simplify the failure-path logging to just check `isSuccess()` and log a generic warning.

